  "goodToKnow": "Die Kreisstadt is a district town, the administrative seat of a Landkreis, where the Landratsamt (district office) is located; many official matters, like car registration, are handled there. Germany has around 300 Landkreise, plus about 100 kreisfreie Städte (independent cities). Car number plates start with district codes, often based on the Kreisstadt, like EBE for Ebersberg. Plural: die Kreisstädte."
